on":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:cd7ae44e9abb42b2167a36890573a683aaa47adbf8f173e409000ebcb4fb29e3","file":"preprints/Lipschitz-Equivalent-Separable-Banach-Spaces-Need-Not-Be-Linearly-Isomorphic-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"10a24811a5f48b6735547303cbabca094000cb6fd0bfe7008aef7aa6d73f8bf4","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Lipschitz-Equivalent-Separable-Banach-Spaces-Need-Not-Be-Linearly-Isomorphic-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:cd7ae44e9abb42b2167a36890573a683aaa47adbf8f173e409000ebcb4fb29e3","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Lipschitz-Equivalent-Separable-Banach-Spaces-Need-Not-Be-Linearly-Isomorphic-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are separable real Banach spaces \\(X,Y\\) and a bijection\n\\(\\Psi:X\\to Y\\) such that, for every \\(s,t\\in X\\),\n\\begin{equation}\n\\label{eq:main-bounds}\n \\frac4{21}\\|s-t\\|_X\n \\le \\|\\Psi(s)-\\Psi(t)\\|_Y\n \\le \\frac{76}{25}\\|s-t\\|_X.\n\\end{equation}\nThe space \\(X\\) contains a linearly isometric copy of \\(c_0(\\ell_2)\\), while\n\\(Y\\) contains no closed subspace linearly isomorphic to\n\\(c_0(\\ell_2)\\). In particular, \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\) are not linearly\nisomorphic."}
